findings.description:
The module docstring promises idempotent writes, but insert_options_snapshot uses a plain INSERT and options_snapshots has no UNIQUE natural key. DataPipeline._snapshot_options does not delete first. The dashboard's startup refresh (which runs whenever the DB is more than 3 days old, which is always, since the tracked DB ends 2026-06-18) and its 4-hourly scheduled refresh (09:00-22:00 ET, i.e. during market hours) both call daily_refresh. Each call appends another full chain under the same snapshot_date, and get_options_surface returns all of them, mixing intraday quote sets. Only cloud_refresh works around this with a manual DELETE.
The schema also drops:
- contractSymbol, although Yahoo's ^SPX chain mixes AM-settled SPX and PM-settled SPXW under the same expiry date;
- the underlying price at quote time;
- the quote timestamp (lastTradeDate).
The 'implied_vol' column is Yahoo's opaque IV and is inconsistent with the stored mids.
